# CellAtria 2.0 — Full Project Status & Issue Summary

## What Is CellAtria 2.0?
An autonomous scRNA-seq drug repurposing pipeline built with **Streamlit + LangGraph + Groq (Llama-3.3-70B) + E2B sandbox**. The user uploads a research paper PDF, and 4 AI agents work in sequence:

```
PDF → Literature Agent → Ingestion Agent → Bioinformatician Agent → Strategist Agent → Drug Candidates
```

| Agent | Role | Current Status |
|-------|------|----------------|
| **Literature Agent** | Extracts GEO accession IDs from PDF (regex + LLM NER) | ✅ Works — finds accessions |
| **Ingestion Agent** | Downloads raw scRNA-seq data from NCBI GEO/FTP | ❌ Downloads timeout (NCBI FTP is slow) |
| **Bioinformatician** | Runs QC pipeline in E2B sandbox | ❌ E2B sandbox constructor fails + no data from ingestion |
| **Strategist** | Runs drug repurposing in E2B sandbox | ❌ E2B sandbox constructor fails + no data upstream |

## The Core Issue (Still Persisting)

**The pipeline times out at 180 seconds and the right panel shows "No drug candidates".**

### Root Cause Chain:

1. **Groq API Rate Limits** — The free-tier Groq API aggressively rate-limits. Each LLM call can trigger 4 retries with exponential backoff (4s→8s→16s→32s = 60s per call). The Literature Agent alone can consume 60s just on rate-limited retries.

2. **NCBI FTP Downloads Hang** — GEOparse fails, raw FTP fallback is slow/times out. Even with a 15s per-accession timeout, the ingestion phase takes 30s+ (2 accessions × 15s).

3. **E2B Sandbox Constructor Error** — The `Sandbox(template=...)` constructor throws `TypeError: SandboxBase.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'template'`. The e2b_code_interpreter SDK version may not match the API being used.

4. **Pipeline Budget Exceeded** — Combined: Literature (60s rate limit) + Ingestion (30s timeouts) + Bioinformatician fallback LLM (60s rate limit) + Strategist fallback LLM (60s rate limit) = **210s > 180s global timeout**. The LLM fallback agents never finish in time.

